{{!
    @template tool_vae/attestations

    The attestation history of a claim: one sentence when there is none, or the list, one line per attestation (one end
    of line after the opening of the list and after each item, as the writer of the core put them): withdrawn, the
    sentence that says so; signed, the role in bold, the statement line by line, the day it was signed, and the day it
    was carried in from an archive.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\attestations. The template holds no logic.
    Every value is escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML. Each line of a statement carries the end of line that
    precedes it, after the break the template draws.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * none - false, or a string: the sentence drawn when there is no attestation
    * hasitems - bool, whether there is a list
    * items - array, each:
        * withdrawn - false, or {text}: the sentence of a withdrawn attestation
        * signed - false, or {role, lines, on, imported}: lines - array of {br (bool), text}; on - string; imported - false
          or {text}

    Example context (json):
    {
        "none": false,
        "hasitems": true,
        "items": [
            {"withdrawn": {"text": "An attestation existed and was withdrawn on 1 June 2026 (Error)."}, "signed": false},
            {"withdrawn": false, "signed": {"role": "Director", "lines": [{"br": false, "text": "I confirm."},
                {"br": true, "text": "\nOn two lines."}], "on": "Signed on 2 June 2026.", "imported": false} }
        ]
    }
}}
{{#none}}
<div class="text-muted">{{none}}</div>
{{/none}}
{{#hasitems}}
<ul class="tool-vae-attestations">
{{#items}}<li>{{#withdrawn}}{{text}}{{/withdrawn}}{{!
}}{{#signed}}<strong>{{role}}</strong><br>{{#lines}}{{#br}}<br>{{/br}}{{text}}{{/lines}}{{!
}}<br><span class="text-muted">{{on}}</span>{{#imported}}<br><span class="text-muted">{{text}}</span>{{/imported}}{{/signed}}</li>
{{/items}}</ul>
{{/hasitems}}
